                <article class="article-content">

                    <!-- SECTION 1: Introduction -->
                    <p class="article-intro"><strong>Dental implants in China</strong> are increasingly considered by international patients who want lower treatment costs without giving up access to major cities, private clinics, or internationally known implant systems. The key question is not only price — it is whether the clinic, implant brand, and treatment plan fit your case and travel timeline.</p>

                    <div class="info-highlight">
                        <h2>Quick cost snapshot</h2>
                        <div class="price-line">From $800 per implant in China</div>
                        <div class="savings-chip">Often 60 to 80% lower than typical US private pricing</div>
                    </div>

                    <h2>Why patients compare dental implant treatment in China</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Lower overall cost</strong>: often much lower than private pricing in the US, UK, or Australia.</li>
                        <li><strong>Wide implant brand choice</strong>: premium and mid-range systems are commonly available.</li>
                        <li><strong>Faster scheduling</strong>: many clinics can see international patients sooner than overloaded local systems.</li>
                        <li><strong>Digital planning</strong>: CT scans, guided surgery, and restorative planning are common in higher-end clinics.</li>
                        <li><strong>Large city options</strong>: Beijing, Shanghai, Guangzhou, and Shenzhen all offer different clinic styles and price levels.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <!-- SECTION 2: Cost Comparison Table -->
                    <h2>Dental implant costs: China vs US vs Thailand vs Mexico (2026)</h2>
                    <p>This comparison covers single implants, full-arch solutions, and supplementary procedures. Prices are typical ranges for planning purposes and vary by clinic, implant brand, and case complexity.</p>
                    <div class="cost-table-wrap">
                        <table class="cost-table">
                            <tr>
                                <th>Procedure</th>
                                <th>China</th>
                                <th>USA</th>
                                <th>Thailand</th>
                                <th>Mexico</th>
                                <th>Typical Savings vs US</th>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>Single Implant <span class="tag">Premium</span></td>
                                <td>$800–$1,500</td>
                                <td>$3,000–$5,000</td>
                                <td>$1,200–$2,000</td>
                                <td>$1,000–$1,800</td>
                                <td><strong>~70%</strong></td>
                            </tr>
