                    </div>
                    <p><em>China pricing is competitive across all procedure types. Thailand and Mexico offer lower costs than the US but typically higher than China for comparable clinic standards. Final quotes vary by implant brand, bone condition, sedation needs, and whether you are comparing a hospital department or a private clinic.</em></p>

                    <!-- SECTION 3: Named Hospital Prices -->
                    <h2>Named dental hospital prices in China</h2>
                    <p>These are hospitals and clinic groups frequently considered by international patients. Price ranges reflect typical quotes for single premium implants and do not include all supplementary costs.</p>
                    <div class="hospital-list">
                        <div class="hospital-card">
                            <h4>Beijing United Family Hospital (JCI Accredited)</h4>
                            <p><strong>Positioning:</strong> International-standard private hospital dental center<br>
                            <strong>City:</strong> Beijing<br>
                            <strong>Single Premium Implant:</strong> $1,200–$1,800<br>
                            <strong>Notes:</strong> English-speaking coordinators, JCI accreditation, familiar private-hospital environment. Often chosen by patients who want international standards at lower cost.</p>
                            <span class="price-tag">From $1,200 per implant</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="hospital-card">
                            <h4>Shanghai Jiao Tong University Dental Hospital</h4>
                            <p><strong>Positioning:</strong> Major academic dental institution<br>
                            <strong>City:</strong> Shanghai<br>
                            <strong>Single Premium Implant:</strong> $900–$1,400<br>
                            <strong>Notes:</strong> High case volume, specialist depth in complex restorations. Relevant for patients comparing large dental institutions.</p>
                            <span class="price-tag">From $900 per implant</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="hospital-card">
                            <h4>Guangzhou Dental Hospital</h4>
                            <p><strong>Positioning:</strong> Established dental hospital in South China<br>
                            <strong>City:</strong> Guangzhou<br>
                            <strong>Single Premium Implant:</strong> $800–$1,300<br>
                            <strong>Notes:</strong> Often considered alongside southern China treatment plans. Broad specialist coverage including oral surgery and prosthodontics.</p>
                            <span class="price-tag">From $800 per implant</span>
                        </div>
